**Motion findings:** motion instants — shot cut to close-up between 1000–1500 ms · pestle strokes: down at ≈2000 · raised at 3000/4000/5000 · down at ≈5500/6000 — a ≈840–1000 ms stroke cycle (down-phase + lift) carried in stop-motion increments (the source is stop-motion throughout: positions jump between frames, no smooth blur). Holds — the wide setup 0–≈1250 ms is a HOLD on the full set; no other true holds: every close-up census instant differs from its predecessor (count down, coverage up). What changes between states: readable count falls monotonically · green coverage rises monotonically · pestle alternates down (centre) / raised (right) · green slabs lose their boundaries (distinct at 1500 → merged by 4000 → invisible as slabs by 5000).
**Sub-beats:** SB-A wide setup hold (full set, pestle at rest) · SB-B close-up entry (pestle raised, set maximal) · SB-C..G strokes 1–5, each collapsing its assigned object cohort · SB-H final paste state (flecks only).
**Fine stroke census (jev-observe-exit charge 1, applied — 250 ms frames `census/fine-*.jpg`, viewed firsthand):** close-up already established at 1250 ms (fine-1250, sha 2289ee1e…) · CONTACT (pestle down, pressing right-of-centre) at 1750 ms (fine-1750, b26e1620…) · down-centre at 2000 ms · RAISED at 2750 ms (fine-2750, ae802931…) · CONTACT down-centre at 3750 ms (fine-3750, fd1b5934…) · CONTACT down-centre at 4750 ms (fine-4750, ed327a50…) with the paste already near-uniform on the left · down at 5500/6000 ms. Binding reading: ≈5 press cycles across 1500–6000 ms at ≈840–1000 ms per cycle. (AMENDED under codex-plan-review: the allocation is 5 × 900 ms with press peaks at 1900/2800/3700/4600/5500 ms — within 150 ms of a sampled contact at 1750–2000/3750/4750/5500; the earlier 840 ms fit's 4398 ms peak stood 352 ms from the nearest contact and was rejected on its face by the review.) **Hold reconciliation:** §1.3's "no other true holds" stands for the SOURCE — the window ends mid-mash at 81.0 s with no source-observed terminal hold; the build's 300 ms end hold (5700–6000 ms) is a DESIGNED hold (the assembler's ending container needs a settled final frame), named here as designed, never as census. Readable/fleck definitions (consistent throughout): readable = object still identifiable by kind at census size; fleck = a colour fragment no longer identifiable by kind.

### 1.4 Variables (§1.3 extraction)
1. Object set — per-object kind (die/house/minidie/cube), position in bowl-relative coords, size, rotation, pip count, collapse-stroke assignment. Counts per kind derived from the array.
2. Collapse law — per-stroke cohort sizes, integrity span (loss inside the assigned stroke), deform coefficients (shrink, corner-rounding, colour blend to paste, sink), fleck size/count (collapsed objects persist as flecks of their own colour).
3. Paste — start coverage, per-stroke coverage growth, paste colours (base/dark), blob geometry (coverage rendered as growing paste field under/over objects).
4. Pestle — geometry (head radii, handle), rest position, raised position, per-stroke target sweep, dip depth, stroke phase split (press vs lift).
5. Bowl/stage — bowl centre/radii, wall colours, board palette, stage size.
6. Labels — input label text, tool label text, output label text, font sizes + family, label positions.
7. Timing — setup duration, stroke count, stroke duration, final hold; phase starts DERIVED sequentially. Stop-motion quantum (stepMs) — the increment size.
8. Palette — board, bowl, paste ×2, die, house, minidie, cube, pestle, ink.
9. Easing — stroke easing name.

### 1.5 Guidance dispositions (inline, A9.5)
- A1 §2 typography precedent: NOT APPLICABLE — no particle typography; labels are SVG text rendered from CONFIG strings.
- A5 Owner Cures 1–2: NOT APPLICABLE as particle/phrase cures — no particle field, no phrase lifecycle. The analogue carried: phase exclusivity by construction — strokes are sequential-derived and an object's collapse cohort belongs to exactly one stroke (no overlapping lifecycles).
- A5 §4 flow-field model: NOT APPLICABLE — no particle pool.
- A9.1 plate construction: NOT APPLICABLE — no moving background plate; the board is still. The moving PESTLE is the tool, priced in §2.1 as tool geometry.
- Family: Packet #13 siblings T232/T233 (Wave 36/37) — receipt-form cures carried binding into §2.3/§2.4 (jev-observe-exit charge 2, citations made explicit): T232's priced cures (`hidden_files/study/recreations/T232-verb-literalization-dicing-dice/scores.md`, "Priced cures" — executable CONFIG expressions on fixed census rows · a MOVED evaluation instant at a census-anchored probe · key-binding receipts) map to T238 §2.3's C@ probes + §2.4's paired timing receipt; T233's priced cure list (`hidden_files/study/recreations/T233-tool-transformation-grid-press/scores.md`, "Priced cure list (for the completion cycle)" — CONFIG-derived companions for fixed probes · full-predicate enforcement over ALL elements · census/config-census reconciliation) maps to T238 §2.3's full-predicate rule over ALL 24 objects + the A13 receipt index in the build-record. In substance: every census probe carries its CONFIG expression · the timing-swap receipt shows a MOVED instant at a census-anchored probe AND the changed value at a fixed census instant · raw phase value and eased result printed separately · every CONFIG key (incl. array-member keys) bound with a swapped-value receipt where a swap touches it.

## §2 — PLAN

### 2.1 Parameter table (every variable → CONFIG key; specimen value = default)
Top-level: `stageW 640 · stageH 400 · bowlCx 320 · bowlCy 208 · bowlRx 218 · bowlRy 104 · bowlWallPx 14 · pasteInsetF 0.92 · pestleRx 64 · pestleRy 42 · pestleRestDx 196 · pestleRestDy -64 · pestleDipPx 34 · pestleLiftPx 26 · pestleHandleLenPx 74 · pestleHandleRxPx 17 · pestleSweepPx 118 · stepMs 100 · pressSteps 4 · pressLossShare 0.7 · readableThresh 0.5 · pasteStart 0.34 · fleckPx 7 · sinkPx 10 · deformShrink 0.55 · deformRound 0.9 · rngSeed 238 · labelFontPx 30 · toolLabelFontPx 28 · inputLabelDy 128 · toolLabelDy -146 · outputLabelDy 128 · fontFamily "Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif" · inputLabel "DICE · HOUSES · CUBES" · toolLabel "PESTLE MASH" · outputLabel "GUACAMOLE" · tSetupMs 0 · setupDurMs 1500 · strokeCount 5 · strokeDurMs 900 · holdMs 0 · easeStroke "easeInOut" · easeSetup "linear" · palette {board #8a6844, boardDark #6f5233, bowl #4a4a48, bowlDark #33322f, paste #79c142, pasteDark #5da334, die #d8262c, dieEdge #8f1218, pip #ffffff, house #159a8c, houseRoof #0d6e64, minidie #f2f2f2, minipip #222222, cube #17b3a6, pestle #55534e, pestleDark #3c3a36, labelInk #ffffff, labelHalo #3a2a18}`. (Schedule AMENDED under codex-plan-review: strokeDurMs 900 fitted to the fine-census contacts — press peaks at 1900/2800/3700/4600/5500 ms, within 150 ms of a sampled contact at 1750–2000/3750/4750/5500; holdMs 0 — completion lands AT the window edge 6000 ms = CP6, no designed hold; pressFrac is replaced by the step-exact pressSteps/stepsPerStroke pair.)
Array: `objects[24]` — `{kind, x, y, s, rot, pips, cs}`: x/y in bowl radii (−1..1), s = size px, cs = collapse stroke 0–4. Kind counts DERIVED: die 8 · house 6 · minidie 6 · cube 4 = 24. Cohort counts DERIVED from cs: 5 · 5 · 5 · 5 · 4 = 24 (count assertion: source cohort sum 24 = built objects.length 24, harness-printed).
Array: `slabs[3]` — `{x, y, rx, ry}` (the three avocado-half slabs of §1.1 priced reading (2), bowl-relative): (-0.52,0.05,0.52,0.78) · (0.05,-0.28,0.55,0.72) · (0.55,0.12,0.50,0.80). Slab scale and union opacity derive from pasteP (below); slab boundary visibility = 1 − pasteP.
Derived (named, never stored): setupEnd=tSetupMs+setupDurMs (=1500) · stepsPerStroke=strokeDurMs/stepMs (=9, validated integer) · pressFrac=pressSteps/stepsPerStroke (=4/9) · strokeStart(k)=setupEnd+k×strokeDurMs (1500/2400/3300/4200/5100) · pressPeak(k)=strokeStart(k)+pressSteps×stepMs (1900/2800/3700/4600/5500) · mashEnd=setupEnd+strokeCount×strokeDurMs (=6000) · completeAtMs=mashEnd (=6000) · durationMs=mashEnd+holdMs (=6000) · **clock (codex-plan-review cure):** the active stroke is derived from RAW t by half-open intervals [strokeStart(k), strokeStart(k+1)) BEFORE quantization; inside the mash the evaluated instant is q = setupEnd + floor((t−setupEnd)/stepMs)×stepMs (q(1500)=1500 exactly; the setup act uses raw t and is NOT quantized — the source wide shot is live-action, named in §2.5) · **press-bound collapse (cure):** per-object loss during its stroke = pressLossShare × (step/pressSteps) for step ≤ pressSteps, then pressLossShare + (1−pressLossShare) × (step−pressSteps)/(stepsPerStroke−pressSteps) — 70% of identity loss rides the press descent, the rest the lift/grind; integrity = 1 − loss (before its stroke 1; after 0 → object renders as a fleck of its own colour) · **kind-marks bound to the same transition (cure):** pip/roof opacity = clamp((integrity − 0.35)/0.65) — the marks that make a kind readable die BEFORE the shape finishes blending, so modeled readability (integrity > readableThresh) never claims marks the state no longer shows · pasteP = pasteStart + (1−pasteStart) × collapsedFraction where collapsedFraction = Σ(1−integrity)/objects.length (denominator DERIVED from the validated nonempty array, never a literal) · readableCount = #{integrity > readableThresh} · fleckCount = #{integrity = 0} · slabScale = 0.55 + 0.75×pasteP · unionOpacity = pasteP · pestle state: setup → rest position (pestleRestDx/Dy), lifting in the setup's second half by pestleLiftPx to the raised pose; during stroke k → target x = bowlCx − pestleSweepPx + 2×pestleSweepPx×sweepFrac(k), sweepFrac = strokeCount>1 ? k/(strokeCount−1) : 0.5 (the strokeCount=1 case handled, cure), y dips by pestleDipPx × pressCurve(step) where pressCurve = step/pressSteps (step ≤ pressSteps) then (stepsPerStroke−step)/(stepsPerStroke−pressSteps); handle = rounded rect of pestleHandleLenPx × 2×pestleHandleRxPx above the head; at/after mashEnd → rests down-centre (the CP6 pose). **Validation:** durations >0; strokeDurMs divisible by stepMs; pressSteps in [1, stepsPerStroke); strokeCount positive integer; pressLossShare in (0,1); readableThresh in (0,1); pasteStart in [0,1); objects nonempty; every cs in [0, strokeCount); object |x|,|y| ≤ 0.92; a violating CONFIG is rejected by validateConfig, never rendered.

### 2.2 Construction choice
**DOM/SVG single-stage scene (chosen):** one SVG; board rect; bowl group (outer wall ellipse + inner paste field); paste layer (codex-plan-review cure — the slab model): the 3 CONFIG slab ellipses (paste fill) scaled by slabScale with their boundaries visible early + a unifying paste ellipse whose opacity = unionOpacity, so slab boundaries are LOST as pasteP → 1 exactly as the census shows (distinct slabs at 1500 → merged by 4000 → invisible by 5000) + pasteDark texture blobs (seeded, positions derived from object index); objects layer — per object a group (die: rounded rect + pip circles · house: rect + roof polygon · minidie: small rect + dark pips · cube: rect) transformed by integrity (scale toward deformShrink floor then fleck, corner radius toward deformRound, fill blended toward paste, y sunk by sinkPx × (1−integrity), kind-marks — pips/roofs — fading on the marks curve, which reaches 0 at integrity 0.35, before the shape finishes blending); pestle group (ellipse head + handle rect) positioned by the stroke machine, drawn ABOVE the objects (real occlusion at stroke bottoms); three CONFIG label texts with EXCLUSIVE ownership (cure): input label opacity = 1 while collapsedFraction < 0.5 else 0, output label opacity = the complement — exactly one owns the stage at any instant (the A5 phase-exclusivity analogue; the harness asserts never both > 0); tool label rides above the bowl at toolLabelDy. All geometry from `stateAt(cfg,t)`, a pure function evaluable in node.
Rejected: Canvas 2D — loses per-element ink measurement the A6 fit leg needs. CSS keyframes — phase state not evaluable as a pure function (A11 receipts impossible). Photographic/generated imagery — approaches the specimen; the technique is the per-stroke identity loss, carried by geometry.
**Named deferrals (lawful, priced):** (1) Hands — not built; the pestle moves by its own stroke machine (fleet diagram form for performed-action techniques, T233 precedent). (2) The wide→close-up shot cut (1000–1500 ms) is compressed onto the single stage: the build's setup act shows the same bowl at stage scale throughout (no zoom); the census cut is a camera change, not a state change — the STATE at 1500 (full set, pestle raised) is what the build binds. (3) The prior technique's chess pieces (CP0/CP1 left foreground) — set dressing of T14, omitted. (4) Texture realism of the stone bowl/paste — flat CONFIG colours + seeded dark blobs stand in for photographic texture; the technique priced is the collapse law, not the material render.

### 2.3 Census-anchor mapping (A10.2) + A11 assertions
Window-start offset: **segment-anchored** — build instant = census seg-rel ms exactly (offset 0). Departure table: CP0/CP1's wide-shot framing + chess dressing have no build counterpart (deferrals §2.2 (2)(3)); their BOUND STATE (readable = all 24, pasteP = pasteStart, pestle at rest) is the build's setup state.
Assertions (CONFIG expression → evaluated instant; receipts print raw phase + eased separately, full predicates over ALL objects; all expected values derived from the AMENDED clock: stepsPerStroke 9, pressSteps 4, pressLossShare 0.7):
- P0 setup start: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tSetupMs)` → 0 ms: readable 24, flecks 0, pasteP = pasteStart (0.34), pestle at rest offset, input label owns stage (output opacity 0).
- P1 setup mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tSetupMs + CONFIG.setupDurMs/2)` → 750 ms: readable 24, strokeIdx −1 (no stroke yet).
- P2 mash start (CP1500 anchor): `stateAt(CONFIG, setupEnd)` → 1500 ms: q = 1500 exactly, readable 24, pestle raised (liftP = 1), strokeIdx 0, step 0.
- P3 stroke-0 press mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, setupEnd + 2×CONFIG.stepMs)` → 1700 ms: step 2, loss = 0.7×2/4 = 0.35, cs-0 integrity 0.65 (raw), marks opacity = (0.65−0.35)/0.65 ≈ 0.4615, readable 24.
- P4 stroke-0 press peak: `stateAt(CONFIG, setupEnd + CONFIG.pressSteps×CONFIG.stepMs)` → 1900 ms: step 4, pressCurve = 1 (dip maximal), cs-0 loss 0.7, integrity 0.3, readable 19.
- C@2000 (CP2): `stateAt(CONFIG, 2000)` → strokeIdx 0, step 5, phase 5/9 ≈ 0.5556, loss = 0.7+0.3×1/5 = 0.76, cs-0 integrity 0.24, readable 19 (census ≈20).
- C@3000 (CP3): strokeIdx 1, step 6, loss = 0.7+0.3×2/5 = 0.82, readable 14 (census ≈18 — the §2.5 tension, printed beside, never fudged).
- C@4000 (CP4): strokeIdx 2, step 7, loss = 0.7+0.3×3/5 = 0.88, readable 9 (census ≈10).
- C@5000 (CP5): strokeIdx 3, step 8, loss = 0.7+0.3×4/5 = 0.94, readable 4 (census ≈6).
- C@5500 (F-5500): strokeIdx 4, step 4 (= press peak of stroke 4), loss 0.7, readable 0, flecks 20 (census: flecks only ✓).
- P5 complete = CP6 anchor: `stateAt(CONFIG, completeAtMs)` → 6000 ms: readable 0, flecks 24, pasteP 1, unionOpacity 1, slab boundaries 0, output label owns stage. **Departure printed:** the specimen at 81.0 s still shows ≈1 partially readable red die at the top edge (it would fall to a stroke beyond the window); the build completes the collapse AT the window edge — guards cmd 8's zero-state probe binds the BUILD's prescribed end state, and the departure is named here, not hidden.
- P6 post-complete identity: `stateAt(CONFIG, completeAtMs + 150)` fully equal to P5 state — RAW FULL-STATE equality over the whole state object (the comparison clamp holds this state; it is not a source hold). durationMs = 6000.
- P7 quantization: `stateAt(CONFIG, 2001)` equals `stateAt(CONFIG, 2000)` on every mash-derived field (same stepMs bucket, q = 2000) AND `stateAt(CONFIG, 2100)` has step 6 ≠ step 5 — the stop-motion increment is executable, not asserted.
- P8 label exclusivity: at every probed instant, inputOpacity × outputOpacity = 0 and inputOpacity + outputOpacity = 1 (exactly one label owns the stage).
- Zero-state anchor (guards cmd 8): the END state is the zero-identity anchor — at P5, readableCount = 0 evaluated from the CONFIG expression `Σ (integrity > readableThresh)` printed raw, not a bare constant.

### 2.4 Verification plan (instruments named)
- Execute checklist: (1) cut segment.mp4 from source.mp4 at 74.5–81.5 s (window ±0.5 handles), libx264/yuv420p + AAC faststart, ffprobe filed; (2) build recreation.html (CONFIG at top, pure stateAt, window.__T238 exposed); (3) build comparison.html — shared controls drive both sides, labels verbatim: "ORIGINAL — PES \"Fresh Guacamole\" @ 75–81 s" · "RECREATION — T238 Identity collapse: pestle mash, parameterized" · sync: ONE shared start timestamp drives both sides; the video (7.0 s cut) maps to build clamp((videoT−0.5)×1000, 0, durationMs) while it plays — the cut starts at 74.5, build zero at source 75.0 = cut-relative 0.5 s; end-of-clip: video ends at wall 7.0 s = build 6500 > durationMs 6000, so the build completes at wall 6.5 s and holds its P5/P6 state while the video plays its last 0.5 s handle — the comparison check tests the build hold at wall 7.0 s · durationMs DERIVED at runtime from recreation.html's CONFIG · phone stacking @media ≤560px; (4) own checks §5 legs 1–3 + A6 legs.
- Swap test: content — inputLabel→"BUTTONS · BEADS · COINS", outputLabel→"PÂTÉ", objects[0].kind "die"→"house" (receipt: kind counts die 8→7, house 6→7 in stateAt census); timing — `strokeDurMs 900→1200` (stepsPerStroke 9→12, pressSteps unchanged 4), PAIRED receipt: (a) at the fixed census instant C@4000 the evaluated state changes — default strokeIdx 2 step 7 loss 0.88 readable 9 → swapped strokeIdx 2 (start 3900) step 1, loss = 0.7×1/4 = 0.175, cs-2 integrity 0.825, readable 19 — AND (b) the corresponding event's shifted instant — stroke-2 start moves 3300→3900 ms (`setupEnd + 2×strokeDurMs` printed at both values), press peak 3700→4300, completeAt 6000→7500; the swapped completion is receipted STANDALONE in the harness (state at 7500 complete) because 7500 lies beyond the comparison's window (codex-plan-review cure); palette — `palette.paste #79c142→#c8b13a` (observed paste fill in stateAt/stub-DOM output).
- Purity: guards cmd1 grep `segment\.mp4|source\.mp4|<video|<img|DnjdJiwcfY` on recreation.html → specimen hits 0 (`url(#id)` in-file refs classified, not counted); asset inventory = recreation.html alone.
- A6 legs: fit-table.md (PIL rendered measurement, stand-in font DejaVu Sans Bold named — measured ink bounds for the 3 CONFIG labels at their CONFIG fonts, at the 360 px stage, INCLUDING the swapped label set) + config-census.md (all literals classified; every CONFIG key incl. `objects[].kind/x/y/s/rot/pips/cs` and `palette.*` resolved to value-flowing sites; CSS-variable check — none used).
- jev-prewave after legs 1–3 + A6, payload per its contract (build-record + CONFIG + fit-table + config-census verbatim per A10.1, binding census-anchor mapping §2.3); five-lens Codex wave (motion · timing · purity · reusability · readability) only on FIRE-WAVE; bar avg ≥85, min ≥70.

### 2.5 Failure points (priced)
- **Census-count tension (named in §2.3):** the specimen's readable count at 3000/5000 ms runs ≈3–4 higher than a strict per-stroke integrity law gives, because partially mashed objects still read. Mitigation priced: integrity's readable threshold is 0.5 and deform (round/blend/sink) is progressive, so a mid-stroke object is visibly degraded — the motion/timing lenses judge the LAW's fidelity; if they price the count gap, the cure is a collapseSpan > 1 stroke (integrity loss spanning into the next stroke), named here as the first cure candidate.
- **Morph-vs-increment reading:** smooth per-object deform could read as a morph, betraying stop-motion. The stepMs quantization binds ALL mash motion to 120 ms increments; P7 asserts it executably.
- **Paste-coverage honesty:** coverage must come from collapsed fraction (Σ integrity), never an independent timeline — a paste that grows on its own clock while objects stay readable is the named defect; stateAt derives pasteP from the objects, by construction.
- **Fleck persistence:** collapsed objects must persist as colour flecks (the specimen's end state is flecked, not clean) — fleckCount = collapsed count, asserted at P5.
- **Label fitting:** longest labels ("DICE · HOUSES · CUBES" 21 chars at labelFontPx 30, swap "BUTTONS · BEADS · COINS" 23 chars) measured in the fit leg at the 360 px stage; a measured overflow is cured in CONFIG font size only.
- **Pestle occlusion:** at stroke bottoms the pestle head covers centre objects — in the specimen this is real occlusion; the build draws the pestle above the objects layer, priced as faithful.
- **Render-proof limitation:** no browser binary in this seat — PIXEL-UNVERIFIED carried to scores.md; comparison page is the render surface.
- **End-state departure (named, §2.3 P5):** the specimen's ≈1 surviving partial die at 81.0 s vs the build's completed collapse at the window edge; a timing/motion lens pricing the specimen's literal end state is answered by this naming — the alternative (leaving one object at integrity ≈0.4 forever) would falsify the technique's own claim (identity collapse completes) for a window-edge accident.
- **Plateau (A2):** FIRST ATTEMPT — no prior average. **Predicted minimum lens: motion fidelity** — hypothesis: the specimen's strokes are hand-driven circular grinds with irregular targets while the build's are a regular left→right sweep, and the census-count tension (§2.3) may also price there; if the wave's minimum is another lens, the WHY in scores.md names it.

