### 2.2 Construction choice
**DOM/SVG single-stage scene (chosen):** one SVG; board rect; bowl group (outer wall ellipse + inner paste field); paste layer (codex-plan-review cure — the slab model): the 3 CONFIG slab ellipses (paste fill) scaled by slabScale with their boundaries visible early + a unifying paste ellipse whose opacity = unionOpacity, so slab boundaries are LOST as pasteP → 1 exactly as the census shows (distinct slabs at 1500 → merged by 4000 → invisible by 5000) + pasteDark texture blobs (seeded, positions derived from object index); objects layer — per object a group (die: rounded rect + pip circles · house: rect + roof polygon · minidie: small rect + dark pips · cube: rect) transformed by integrity (scale toward deformShrink floor then f
Rejected: Canvas 2D — loses per-element ink measurement the A6 fit leg needs. CSS keyframes — phase state not evaluable as a pure function (A11 receipts impossible). Photographic/generated imagery — approaches the specimen; the technique is the per-stroke identity loss, carried by geometry.
**Named deferrals (lawful, priced):** (1) Hands — not built; the pestle moves by its own stroke machine (fleet diagram form for performed-action techniques, T233 precedent). (2) The wide→close-up shot cut (1000–1500 ms) is compressed onto the single stage: the build's setup act shows the same bowl at stage scale throughout (no zoom); the census cut is a camera change, not a state change — the STATE at 1500 (full set, pestle raised) is what the build binds. (3) The prior technique's chess pieces (CP0/CP1 left foreground) — set dressing of T14, omitted. (4) Texture realism of the stone bowl/paste — flat CONFIG colours + seeded dark blobs stand in for photographic texture; the technique priced is the collapse law, not the material 

### 2.3 Census-anchor mapping (A10.2) + A11 assertions
Window-start offset: **segment-anchored** — build instant = census seg-rel ms exactly (offset 0). Departure table: CP0/CP1's wide-shot framing + chess dressing have no build counterpart (deferrals §2.2 (2)(3)); their BOUND STATE (readable = all 24, pasteP = pasteStart, pestle at rest) is the build's setup state.
