19:### Priced gap (what attempt 2 must cure — OWNER items at the head, then the returns)
21:**OWNER CURE 1 — foreground/background intensity separation (owner's read, 2026-11-14; no lens named it):** word particles and reserve particles currently render at the SAME intensity, so the formed word fights its own background and reads poorly. Cure: borrowed (word) particles render FOREGROUND — separated contrast/opacity/intensity; reserve particles render BACKGROUND — dimmer. In the original this separation is part of why the words read at all.
23:**OWNER CURE 2 — strict phrase sequencing (owner's read, 2026-11-14; no lens named it):** the next phrase can begin forming while the current one is still mid-lifecycle — overlapping animations. Cure: phase exclusivity in the scheduler — a phrase's formation begins only after the previous phrase's dissolve completes; one lifecycle owns the stage at a time.
25:**Construction model for cures 1 + 2 + priced cure 1 below (HQ's note, standing):** ONE constant flow field — every particle always carries stream velocity; forming = borrowing particles onto targets (low-amplitude jitter, never zero velocity; a guaranteed reserve fraction is never borrowed); dissolving = releasing back to full stream velocity with continuity. Intensity rides the borrow flag.
27:1. **Streaming reserve + velocity continuity** (motion 68; reuse concurs on the freeze; SUBSUMED into the flow-field model above): surplus particles currently freeze during FORM (targets = start positions) and the largest phrase leaves zero residual dust during HOLD. Cure: a config-sized reserve share of the pool never takes letterform targets and always streams; velocities persist across phase changes instead of resetting at DISSOLVE→GAP.
28:2. **Surplus/pool policy** (reuse 64): pool never shrinks after a dense phrase. Cure: configurable surplus policy (drift-off + fade, or capped ambient count).
29:3. **Fitting bounds** (reuse 64): font fit stops ~14 px with no wrap/height fit — long phrases can clip. Cure: bounded width-AND-height fit with multiline wrap as a config option.
30:4. **Config validation** (reuse 64): zero durations can NaN; sampleGap 0 hangs; empty phrase array unguarded. Cure: clamp/validate all numeric config at load; guard empty phrases.
31:5. **Original-tempo preset** (timing 82): default brisk variant (1.5/1.5/1.3) vs original proportions 40:33:27. Cure: ship `preset: "original"` (3000/2500/2000) as the default config and keep "brisk" as a named variant.
32:6. **Determinism on restart** (reuse 64): restart does not reset RNG/positions. Cure: restart re-seeds and rebuilds the pool.
37:Per the owner's refinement (2026-11-13), re-attempts belong to the practice job — and T15, as the lane's only scored recreation, is its first pick under the lowest-scored rule. Seed order: **OWNER cures 1–2 first** (they are also the flow-field rebuild that carries priced cure 1), then priced cures 2–6 (surplus policy · fit bounds · config validation · tempo preset · restart determinism). **Attempt 2 is scored by FIVE lenses** (readability added 2026-11-14) — its average is a different instrument from attempt 1's four-lens 78.5; the delta prints both lens counts. Floor rule binds: if attempt 2 does not beat 78.5, it files WHY here (plateau named).
