fficients) are subject-shaping, not structural, whenever changing them changes what the subject looks like; font-family stacks named in CSS are likewise subject-shaping (typography is a shaping decision) and must be CONFIG keys or be classified HIT — a census that passes either class as "structural" has missed its own class. **Addendum landed 2026-11-16 (recreation Cycle 021 Condense, under codex-condense REVISE — invariant-exemption bar):** the declared-invariant classification is barred for any literal that implements a dimension a CONFIG key promises — if a geom.* key names it, the literals constructing it are subject-shaping and must read from the key. Forcing evidence: T130 (Cycle 021) — the car silhouette path coordinates and wheel offsets were exempted as declared invariants while geom.carW/carH promised that control; reusability lens 68.
